Third-party components
----------------------
- Interface icons: Lucide 1.59.0 (https://lucide.dev), ISC License,
  Copyright (c) 2026 Lucide Icons and Contributors; parts derived from
  Feather (MIT), Copyright (c) 2013-present Cole Bemis. A subset is embedded
  as assets/fonts/icons.ttf; the full license is in
  packaging/icons/LICENSE-lucide.
File Explorer is built with many open-source Rust crates, each under its
own license (MIT, Apache-2.0, or similar); `cargo license` lists them. The
optional search index adds these, which are compiled into the program:

- SQLite (public domain), https://sqlite.org
- SQLCipher Community Edition, Copyright (c) 2008-2020 Zetetic LLC,
  BSD-style license (reproduced in full below),
  https://www.zetetic.net/sqlcipher/
- OpenSSL (Windows builds only, linked statically for SQLCipher's
  encryption), Apache License 2.0, https://www.openssl.org
  Linux and FreeBSD builds use the system's libcrypto; macOS builds use
  Apple's CommonCrypto.
- RustCrypto argon2, chacha20poly1305 and blake2 (MIT or Apache-2.0).
- Place names for photo locations: GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org),
  licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), via the reverse_geocoder
  crate (MIT or Apache-2.0). The data is used unmodified.
- kamadak-exif, for photo dates and positions, BSD-2-Clause license
  (reproduced in full below).
- llama.cpp and ggml (smart search), Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml
  authors, MIT License (reproduced in full below), linked statically via
  the llama-cpp-2 crates (MIT or Apache-2.0).
- Model downloads use ureq and rustls (MIT or Apache-2.0), ring (Apache-2.0
  and ISC) and webpki-roots (CDLA-Permissive-2.0 for the root certificates).
- The models themselves are not included; they are downloaded on request:
  BGE small en v1.5 by BAAI (MIT License),
  https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5, and granite-docling-258M
  by IBM (Apache License 2.0), https://huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granite-docling-258M,
  both in the GGUF conversions published by ggml-org, and Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct
  by the Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud (Apache License 2.0),
  https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct, in Qwen's own GGUF
  conversion.
- The keyring-core credential-store crates (MIT or Apache-2.0).

